{{Infobox government agency|agency_name=Secretariat of Transport and Communications|nativename=Secretaria de Transports y Comunicacions|logo=STC logo.svg|logo_width=250px|logo_caption=|seal=|seal_width=|seal_caption=|formed={{Start date and age|1885|3|22|df=yes}}|preceding1=|dissolved=|superseding=|jurisdiction=[[Government and politics of Balisca|Government of Balisca]]|headquarters=[[Castejón]], Balisca|coordinates=|employees=|budget=|minister1_name=[[Miliano Gutiérrez]]|minister1_pfo=Secretary of Transport and Communications|chief1_name=|chief1_position=|chief2_name=|chief2_position=|parent_agency=|child1_agency=|child2_agency=|website=|footnotes=[[Secretariat Council (Balisca)|List of Baliscan secretariats]]|minister2_pfo=|minister2_name=}}The '''Secretariat of Transport and Communications''' ({{Lang-bl|Secretaria de Transports y Comunicacions}}) is a [[Balisca|Baliscan]] [[Secretariat Council (Balisca)|secretariat]] established in 1885. It is responsible for overseeing the implementation of [[Confederal initiative|confederal initiatives]], especially regarding policy and regulation of transportation and communications networks and administration of all trans-regional transportation and communications operations and enterprises in the confederation. 

